<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 213)</h2>
<p><b>Kitsu integration.</b> The review list builds itself from the tracker.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>File ▸ Review List from Kitsu…</b> — pick a project and every shot task awaiting review arrives as a clip, named <code>SEQ_SHOT_vNNN</code>. The last two versions of each come down, grouped per shot, so "what changed?" is one keypress from the moment the list opens.</li>
<li><b>Kitsu's own playlists pull too</b> — listed newest-first, and they arrive in the curator's running order, exactly as built in Kitsu.</li>
<li>Status filter defaults to <code>wfa, Review, pndng</code> and is editable — your studio's vocabulary, not ours.</li>
<li>Auth is a Kitsu <b>bot token</b> in your keychain (the manual has the two-line setup). Works over Tailscale/VPN; previews download once into a local cache.</li>
<li><b>Choose where downloads live</b> — Settings ▸ Playback ▸ Downloaded media location points Kitsu previews and Open-from-Link downloads at any folder, like a fast external drive.</li>
</ul>
<p>Also: a clip's rendering colour space now comes from the per-media-type choice directly, so nothing external can flip an open QuickTime to scene-linear.</p>
]]></description>
